# ===========================================================
# CODING STANDARDS
# ===========================================================

## TypeScript
- Strict mode ON. Zero `any` types — use `unknown` and narrow it
- All functions have explicit return types
- `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/primitives
- Entity types live in src/types/models.ts
- API response shapes in src/types/api.types.ts
- Use optional chaining ?. and nullish coalescing ?? everywhere

## Components
- Functional components only — no class components
- PascalCase file names: TaskCard.tsx
- kebab-case folder names: /features/task-board/
- Max 200 lines per component — split if longer
- Never fetch data directly in JSX — delegate to a custom hook
- Never call API functions in event handlers — go through hooks
- Named exports for components, default exports for pages only

## Colocation Rule
- Used in one feature only → components/features/[feature]/
- Used in 2+ features → promote to components/common/
- Hook used in one component → can live next to it
- Hook used in 2+ places → promote to hooks/


# ===========================================================
# API LAYER — LARAVEL BACKEND
# ===========================================================
# UPDATE whenever the backend adds endpoints or changes the
# API contract. Keep in sync with Postman collection.

## Base Setup
- Base URL from process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL (example: http://localhost:8000/api/v1)
- Never hardcode URLs — always use constants from lib/constants/config.ts
- Required headers on every request (unless backend says otherwise):
  - Accept: application/json
  - X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

## Axios Interceptors (src/lib/api/axios.ts)
- Request: send cookies (`withCredentials`) and CSRF header if required by backend
- Response 401: optional refresh → retry once → redirect to /login
- Response 403: toast "You don't have permission" — do NOT redirect
- Response 422: parse validation errors → structured error object for RHF
- Response 500: toast "Server error, try again" + log to monitoring

## API Contract Expectations
- Pagination: { data: T[], meta: { total, per_page, current_page, last_page } }
- Errors:     { message: string, errors: { [field]: string[] } }
- Success:    { data: T, message?: string }
- Dates:      ISO 8601 strings — always parse with date-fns

## Current Endpoint Map
# UPDATE this table as the backend dev ships endpoints
# Status: Pending | Ready | Integrated

| Method | Endpoint                      | Status   | Hook             |
|--------|-------------------------------|----------|------------------|
| POST   | /auth/login                   | Pending  | useAuth          |
| POST   | /auth/logout                  | Pending  | useAuth          |
| GET    | /auth/me                      | Pending  | useAuth          |
| GET    | /projects                     | Pending  | useProjects      |
| POST   | /projects                     | Pending  | useProjects      |
| GET    | /projects/:id                 | Pending  | useProject       |
| PUT    | /projects/:id                 | Pending  | useProject       |
| DELETE | /projects/:id                 | Pending  | useProject       |
| GET    | /projects/:id/tasks           | Pending  | useTasks         |
| POST   | /tasks                        | Pending  | useTasks         |
| PUT    | /tasks/:id                    | Pending  | useTask          |
| DELETE | /tasks/:id                    | Pending  | useTask          |
| GET    | /users/team                   | Pending  | useTeam          |
| GET    | /notifications                | Pending  | useNotifications |
| GET    | /calendar/events              | Pending  | useCalendar      |
| POST   | /proposals                    | Pending  | useProposals     |
| GET    | /proposals/:id/export         | Pending  | useProposals     |

## TanStack Query Rules
- All query keys in src/lib/constants/query-keys.ts (factory pattern)
- Always handle isLoading, isError, isEmpty in UI — never skip these
- invalidateQueries after every successful mutation
- staleTime guide:
  - User profile: 10 minutes
  - Projects list: 2 minutes
  - Task boards: 30 seconds
  - Notifications: 15 seconds


# ===========================================================
# STATE MANAGEMENT
# ===========================================================
# TanStack Query owns ALL server state.
# Zustand owns ONLY client/UI state.
# Never duplicate server data in Zustand.

## Zustand Stores
# UPDATE when a new store is created — document what it owns

### auth.store.ts
Owns: user object, isAuthenticated, role
Does NOT own: tokens (httpOnly cookie), permissions logic

### ui.store.ts
Owns: sidebarOpen, activeModal, theme (light/dark)
Does NOT own: any server data

### notification.store.ts
Owns: unreadCount, isNotificationPanelOpen
Does NOT own: notification list data (that is React Query)


# ===========================================================
# FORMS & VALIDATION
# ===========================================================

- Every form: React Hook Form + Zod schema
- Zod schemas: src/lib/validations/[feature].schema.ts
- RHF mode: onBlur (not onChange)
- Always show field-level error messages below each input
- Mark required fields with * in label
- Disable submit button while isPending — show spinner inside button
- Map Laravel 422 errors to RHF field errors via response interceptor
- Multi-step forms: show "Step N of N" progress bar


# ===========================================================
# SECURITY STANDARDS
# ===========================================================
# Non-negotiable. Highest priority rules.
# UPDATE immediately when auth strategy or policies change.

## Authentication
- Tokens: httpOnly + Secure + SameSite=Strict cookies ONLY
  Set via Next.js API route /api/auth/login
  NEVER localStorage, NEVER sessionStorage
- Token refresh: silent refresh on 401 → retry → redirect on failure
- Logout: POST /api/auth/logout → clear cookie → clear Zustand state
- Session expiry: modal warning at 5 min remaining

## RBAC
- Roles: admin | manager | member | viewer
- usePermissions() hook: canCreate, canEdit, canDelete, canManageTeam
- VIEWER role: HIDE action buttons entirely (not just disabled)
- Admin routes: protected in middleware.ts by role check
- UI RBAC is for UX only — backend always enforces real access

## Input Sanitization
- DOMPurify on ALL user-generated content rendered as HTML
- Never dangerouslySetInnerHTML without DOMPurify
- All inputs validated with Zod before API submission

## Request Security
- CSRF token header on all mutating requests (Sanctum)
- axios.defaults.withCredentials = true
- Rate-limit login: disable button 30s after 5 failures

## Security Headers (next.config.js)
- X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
- X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
- Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
- Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
- Content-Security-Policy: defined in next.config.js

## Sensitive Data Rules
- Never log PII to console
- Never pre-fill password fields from stored values
- Exports: stream from server, never assemble client-side fully
- Never expose user ID or role in URL params

## Dependencies
- npm audit before every deployment — fix HIGH/CRITICAL immediately
- Pin major versions in package.json


# ===========================================================
# UI/UX STANDARDS
# ===========================================================

## Visual Hierarchy
- One primary CTA per page (shadcn variant="default")
- Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48px (p-1 through p-12)
- Always left-align body text and table data — never center
- Group content with whitespace, not just borders

## Typography Scale
- Page title:      text-2xl font-semibold
- Section header:  text-lg font-medium
- Body / labels:   text-sm
- Meta / captions: text-xs text-muted-foreground
- Max 2 font weights per page

## Color Tokens
Use shadcn semantic tokens only — never raw hex in classNames
- Text:     text-foreground / text-muted-foreground
- Surfaces: bg-background / bg-card / bg-muted
- Borders:  border
- Danger:   text-destructive / bg-destructive
- Brand:    text-primary / bg-primary

## Task/Project Status Colors
# UPDATE if statuses are added or renamed
- Todo:        bg-slate-100  text-slate-600
- In Progress: bg-blue-100   text-blue-700
- In Review:   bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700
- Done:        bg-green-100  text-green-700
- Blocked:     bg-red-100    text-red-700

## Loading States
- Every data-fetching component MUST have a Skeleton matching its shape
- Never full-page spinners — skeleton the content region only
- Mutations: disable button + spinner inside
- 200ms minimum delay before skeleton (prevents flicker on fast connections)

## Empty States
- Every list, table, and board MUST have a designed empty state
- Structure: Lucide icon (size=48) + heading + subtext + CTA button
- Use text-muted-foreground for copy

## Feedback & Micro-interactions
- All actions: immediate visual feedback < 100ms
- Success: toast.success() — auto-dismiss 3s
- Error: toast.error() — persist, show retry if relevant
- Destructive actions: ALWAYS confirmation dialog first
- Use optimistic updates for status changes and drag-drop reordering

## Tables
- Required: column sorting, row hover, skeleton, empty state
- Show: "Showing 1–20 of 143 results"
- Truncate long cells with truncate + Tooltip for full text
- Sticky header on scroll
- Bulk actions: floating action bar above table

## Modals
- Always use shadcn Dialog — never a custom modal
- Always X close button top-right
- Form modals: do NOT close on backdrop click (data loss risk)
- shadcn built-in transitions only

## Confirmations
- Destructive dialog must name exactly what will be deleted
- Provide Undo via Sonner toast (5s window) before permanent action


# ===========================================================
# MOBILE RESPONSIVENESS
# ===========================================================

## Breakpoints
- base (0–639px):  Mobile — single column, stacked, full-width
- sm   (640px+):   Large mobile tweaks
- md   (768px+):   Tablet — 2-column where appropriate
- lg   (1024px+):  Desktop — sidebar + content layout
- xl   (1280px+):  Wide desktop

## Navigation
- Desktop: fixed left sidebar 240px wide
- Mobile:  sidebar as slide-over shadcn Drawer via hamburger
- Mobile bottom nav: 4 icon tabs (Dashboard, Projects, Tasks, Calendar)

## Layout Rules
- Never fixed pixel widths — use w-full max-w-[X] mx-auto
- Tables: wrap in overflow-x-auto w-full div
- Cards: grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3
- Forms: single column always on mobile

## Touch Targets
- All interactive elements: minimum 44x44px (min-h-11 min-w-11)
- List item links: py-3 px-4 minimum padding
- Drag-and-drop: enable @dnd-kit pointer sensor for touch

## Input Types for Mobile Keyboards
- Email: type="email"
- Phone: type="tel"
- Numbers: type="number"
- URL: type="url"

## Heavy Views on Mobile
- Gantt: list view on mobile (< md), Gantt on md+
  Pattern: hidden md:block / block md:hidden
- Task tables: card-stack as mobile alternative

## Performance on Mobile
- Lazy-load heavy components via dynamic():
  Gantt, FullCalendar, export modals, rich text editors
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion
- loading="lazy" on all below-fold images
- Test on throttled 3G before marking complete


# ===========================================================
# ACCESSIBILITY (WCAG 2.1 AA)
# ===========================================================

- All interactive elements: keyboard-navigable + visible focus ring
- All images: descriptive alt text
- Semantic HTML: nav, main, aside, section, article, button
- Never div/span as clickable without role and tabIndex
- Color contrast: AA minimum — verify all custom colors
- Never convey info through color alone — pair with icon or label
- ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
- Focus trap in open modals (shadcn handles this — do not override)


# ===========================================================
# PERFORMANCE
# ===========================================================

- Lazy-load heavy components with dynamic():
  const GanttView = dynamic(() => import('../gantt/GanttView'), { ssr: false })
- React.memo for expensive list item components
- useMemo / useCallback only for proven bottlenecks — not by default
- Next.js Image component for all images
- Paginate ALL lists — never fetch unlimited records
- Prefetch on hover for predictable navigation routes


# ===========================================================
# TESTING
# ===========================================================

- Vitest + React Testing Library
- Test files colocated: ComponentName.test.tsx next to component
- Required per feature:
  - Happy path (data loads, renders correctly)
  - Loading state renders skeleton
  - Empty state renders when no data
  - Error state shows error message
  - Form validation blocks submission with invalid data
- Mock API calls with MSW (Mock Service Worker)
- Never test implementation details — test behavior only


# ===========================================================
# NAMING CONVENTIONS
# ===========================================================
# UPDATE when new file types or patterns are introduced

| Thing              | Convention               | Example                  |
|--------------------|--------------------------|--------------------------|
| Components         | PascalCase               | TaskCard.tsx             |
| Page files         | lowercase                | page.tsx, layout.tsx     |
